From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt7603: reset PSE after a repeated beacon stall

The light reset cannot always drain a leaked beacon token.  If the beacon
stall recurs, use the existing full PSE reset path while DMA is stopped.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
--- a/mt7603/mac.c
+++ b/mt7603/mac.c
@@ -1455,7 +1455,9 @@ static void mt7603_mac_work(struct work
 	}
 
 	if (dev->reset_cause[RESET_CAUSE_RESET_FAILED] ||
-	    dev->cur_reset_cause == RESET_CAUSE_RX_PSE_BUSY)
+	    dev->cur_reset_cause == RESET_CAUSE_RX_PSE_BUSY ||
+	    (dev->cur_reset_cause == RESET_CAUSE_BEACON_STUCK &&
+	     dev->reset_cause[RESET_CAUSE_BEACON_STUCK] >= 2))
 		mt7603_pse_reset(dev);
 
 	if (!dev->reset_cause[RESET_CAUSE_RESET_FAILED]) {
